    "issue": 252,
    "image": "grafana/tempo:3.0.2@sha256:cda87c212d8c584dc0b89e337e7ed648a5100feb657e5d528480ee4fa03dbbe3",
    "captured": "2026-08-05",
    "config": "deploy/e2e/tempo.yaml exactly as committed by this change (metrics_generator.storage.path present); without it the reference answers every TraceQL metrics query with no series at all",
    "how": "standalone container on the host, OTLP/HTTP ingest of one resource per corpus (resource.service.name = the corpus's service), then GET /api/metrics/query_range at step=60s over a 20-minute window covering the ingest. Each bucket's `count` is the SUM of that series' samples over the window, so a corpus straddling a step boundary is still recorded exactly; `emitted_buckets` is in the order the reference returned the series, and `wire_text` is the doubleValue text read off the HTTP body (not a re-rendering of a parsed float).",
    "note": "TraceQL metrics visibility lags search visibility by roughly a minute on this build (the live block has to complete), which is why the e2e control polls the reference rather than querying it once",
    "series_order": "`emitted_buckets` order is RECORDED, not matched: PulsusDB emits histogram series ascending by bucket, a ledgered divergence (2026-08-05-traceql-histogram-series-order). Each corpus's reference sequence is pinned as an explicit expectation in tests/traces_log2_reference.rs, so a change on their side fails rather than being absorbed. The reference's order is lexicographic on Go's %g rendering of the label - sortResponse compares AnyValue.String(), which is proto.CompactTextString (pkg/tempopb/common/v1/common.pb.go:46 @ v3.0.2) ending at gogo writeAny's default arm, fmt.Fprint, i.e. Go %v/%g - so it is neither numeric nor the order of its own wire text.",
    "reference_source": "pkg/traceql/engine_metrics.go:2038 Log2Bucketize, :2058 Log2QuantileWithBucket, ast_metrics.go:181 bucketizeDuration, modules/frontend/combiner/metrics_query_range.go:245 sortResponse - all @ v3.0.2 (0c4b926d09234186de39833e9c7ecb5b7614c8b9)"
  },
